   "title": "Section 01: Functions, Modulus, Symmetries & Graph Transformations",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "1.1 Function Mapping Taxonomy"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Injective (One-to-One)**: $f(x_1) = f(x_2) \\implies x_1 = x_2$. Strictly monotonic functions ($f'(x) > 0$ or $f'(x) < 0$ everywhere) are always one-to-one.",
      "**Surjective (Onto)**: $\\text{Range}(f) = \\text{Codomain}(f)$. Every element in target set has at least one pre-image.",
      "**Bijective**: Both injective and surjective. A function has an inverse $f^{-1}(x)$ if and only if it is bijective.",
      "**Horizontal Line Test**: A function is injective if and only if no horizontal line intersects its graph more than once."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "1.2 Modulus & Special Functions"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Modulus $|x|$**: $|x| = x$ if $x \\ge 0$, and $-x$ if $x < 0$. Continuous everywhere; non-differentiable at sharp corner $x = 0$.",
      "**Graph Transformations of Modulus**:",
      "$y = |f(x)|$: Reflect all parts of $f(x)$ lying below the $x$-axis upwards above the $x$-axis.",
      "$y = f(|x|)$: Erase the portion for $x < 0$; reflect the portion for $x \\ge 0$ across the $y$-axis (ensures even symmetry).",
      "$y = |f(|x|)|$: Apply $f(|x|)$ first, then reflect any remaining negative $y$ regions upwards.",
      "**Greatest Integer Function $[x]$ (Floor)**:",
      "Definition: Largest integer $\\le x$. Step discontinuities at every integer $x = k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$.",
      "Identity: $[x] + [-x] = 0$ if $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, and $-1$ if $x otin \\mathbb{Z}$.",
      "**Fractional Part Function $\\{x\\}$**:",
      "Definition: $\\{x\\} = x - [x] \\in [0, 1)$. Periodic with fundamental period $T = 1$. Saw-tooth waveform.",
      "**Signum Function $\\text{sgn}(x)$**:",
      "$\\text{sgn}(x) = +1$ ($x > 0$), $0$ ($x = 0$), $-1$ ($x < 0$). Also $\\text{sgn}(x) = \\frac{x}{|x|} = \\frac{|x|}{x}$ for $x eq 0$. Jump discontinuity of height 2 at $x = 0$."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "1.3 Symmetries & Periodicity"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Even Function**: $f(-x) = f(x)$. Symmetric about the $y$-axis. E.g. $\\cos x, x^2, |x|$.",
      "**Odd Function**: $f(-x) = -f(x)$. Symmetric about the origin (rotational symmetry by $180^\\circ$). E.g. $\\sin x, x^3, \\tan x$.",
      "**Even/Odd Decomposition**: Any function $f(x)$ can be uniquely decomposed as $f(x) = f_e(x) + f_o(x)$ where:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "f_e(x) = \\frac{f(x) + f(-x)}{2}, \\quad f_o(x) = \\frac{f(x) - f(-x)}{2}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Periodic Function**: $f(x + T) = f(x)$ for fundamental period $T > 0$.",
      "Period of $\\sin(ax), \\cos(ax)$: $T = \\frac{2\\pi}{|a|}$. Period of $\\tan(ax)$: $T = \\frac{\\pi}{|a|}$.",
      "Sum of periodic functions $f_1(x) + f_2(x)$: Period $T = \\text{LCM}(T_1, T_2)$ (provided LCM exists; ratio $T_1 / T_2$ must be rational)."
     ]
    }
   ]
