   "id": "section-07-single-variable-definite-integrals-king-queen-reduction",
   "title": "Section 07: Single-Variable Definite Integrals, King/Queen & Reduction",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "7.1 Fundamental Properties of Definite Integrals"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**King's Property**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\int_a^b f(x) dx = \\int_a^b f(a + b - x) dx \\quad \\left( \\text{Special Case } a = 0: \\int_0^a f(x) dx = \\int_0^a f(a - x) dx\night)"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**The 2I Weapon**: If $f(x) + f(a + b - x) = C \\implies I = \\frac{C(b - a)}{2}$.",
      "Classic: $\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sin^n x}{\\sin^n x + \\cos^n x} dx = \\frac{\\pi/2 - 0}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ for ANY power $n$.",
      "**Queen's Property**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\int_0^{2a} f(x) dx = 2\\int_0^a f(x) dx \\quad \\text{if } f(2a - x) = f(x); \\quad \\text{and } 0 \\quad \\text{if } f(2a - x) = -f(x)"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Interval Symmetry on $[-a, a]$**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\int_{-a}^a f(x) dx = 2\\int_0^a f(x) dx \\quad (\\text{if even: } f(-x) = f(x)); \\quad \\text{and } 0 \\quad (\\text{if odd: } f(-x) = -f(x))"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Periodic Function Reduction ($f(x + T) = f(x)$)**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\int_0^{nT} f(x) dx = n \\int_0^T f(x) dx, \\quad \\int_a^{a + nT} f(x) dx = n \\int_0^T f(x) dx, \\quad \\int_{a + nT}^{b + nT} f(x) dx = \\int_a^b f(x) dx"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "7.2 Wallis' Reduction Formulas"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\sin^m x \\cos^n x dx = \\frac{[(m - 1)(m - 3)\\dots][(n - 1)(n - 3)\\dots]}{(m + n)(m + n - 2)(m + n - 4)\\dots} \\times K"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Parity Multiplier $K$**:",
      "$K = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$ if and only if **BOTH $m$ and $n$ are EVEN** non-negative integers.",
      "$K = 1$ otherwise (if either $m$ or $n$ is odd)."
     ]
    }
   ]
