   "id": "section-08-leibniz-differentiation-beta-gamma-arc-length",
   "title": "Section 08: Leibniz Differentiation, Beta-Gamma & Arc Length",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "8.1 Leibniz Rule of Differentiation Under the Integral Sign"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\frac{d}{dx} \\int_{\\phi(x)}^{\\psi(x)} f(x, t) dt = f(x, \\psi(x))\\cdot \\psi'(x) - f(x, \\phi(x))\\cdot \\phi'(x) + \\int_{\\phi(x)}^{\\psi(x)} \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}(x, t) dt"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Fundamental Theorem of Calculus Part 1**: $\\frac{d}{dx}\\int_a^x f(t) dt = f(x)$."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "8.2 Gamma & Beta Special Functions"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Gamma Function**: $\\Gamma(n) = \\int_0^\\infty x^{n-1} e^{-x} dx \\quad (n > 0)$.",
      "Recurrence: $\\Gamma(n + 1) = n \\Gamma(n) = n! \\quad (n \\in \\mathbb{N})$.",
      "Half-Integer: $\\Gamma(1/2) = \\sqrt{\\pi}, \\quad \\Gamma(3/2) = \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi}, \\quad \\Gamma(-1/2) = -2\\sqrt{\\pi}$.",
      "Reflection Formula: $\\Gamma(n) \\Gamma(1 - n) = \\frac{\\pi}{\\sin(n\\pi)}$.",
      "**Beta Function**: $B(m, n) = \\int_0^1 x^{m-1} (1 - x)^{n-1} dx = 2\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\sin^{2m-1}\\theta \\cos^{2n-1}\\theta d\\theta$.",
      "Fundamental Bridge: $B(m, n) = \\frac{\\Gamma(m) \\Gamma(n)}{\\Gamma(m + n)}$.",
      "**Gaussian Integral**: $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty e^{-x^2} dx = \\sqrt{\\pi} \\implies \\int_0^\\infty e^{-a x^2} dx = \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi}{a}}$."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "8.3 Arc Length & Surface Area of Solids of Revolution"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "**Arc Length**:",
      "Cartesian: $s = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{1 + (y')^2} dx$.",
      "Parametric: $s = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{(x')^2 + (y')^2} dt$. (Astroid $x = a\\cos^3 t, y = a\\sin^3 t \\implies s = 6a$).",
      "Polar: $s = \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 + (r')^2} d\\theta$. (Cardioid $r = a(1 + \\cos\\theta) \\implies s = 8a$).",
      "**Volume of Solid of Revolution (about $x$-axis)**: $V = \\pi \\int_a^b [y(x)]^2 dx$.",
      "**Surface Area of Solid of Revolution (about $x$-axis)**: $S = 2\\pi \\int_a^b y \\sqrt{1 + (y')^2} dx$."
     ]
    }
   ]
